features/12-cylinder/final-review-2.md:1446:  If a cylindrical face is trimmed by less than `0.1` rad (~5.7°), this condition still treats it as a full revolution and the UV-grid path emits a closed cylinder instead of rejecting it. Because `t_range` is stored explicitly on each edge, the floating-point noise here should be tiny; using a `0.1`-rad tolerance reintroduces the silent mis-meshing this change is trying to prevent for near-full partial cylinders.
features/12-cylinder/final-review-2.md:1455:  If a cylindrical face is trimmed by less than `0.1` rad (~5.7°), this condition still treats it as a full revolution and the UV-grid path emits a closed cylinder instead of rejecting it. Because `t_range` is stored explicitly on each edge, the floating-point noise here should be tiny; using a `0.1`-rad tolerance reintroduces the silent mis-meshing this change is trying to prevent for near-full partial cylinders.
